          {"study_index": 42, "title": "Prognostic significance of radial margins of clearance in rectal cancer",       
  "abstract": "A retrospective review of 325 patients was undertaken to analyse whether involvement of the radial       
  resection margin (RRM) could predict locally recurrent disease or distant metastases in patients who had curative     
  surgery for rectal or rectosigmoid cancer. Information on the RRM was available in 253 patients. The RRM was          
