          {"study_index": 45, "title": "Preoperative radiotherapy combined with total mesorectal excision for           
  resectable rectal cancer", "abstract": "Background Short-term preoperative radiotherapy and total mesorectal          
  excision have each been shown to improve local control of disease in patients with resectable rectal cancer. We       
  conducted a multicenter, randomized trial to determine whether the addition of preoperative radiotherapy increases    
  the benefit of total mesorectal excision.   Methods We randomly assigned 1861 patients with resectable rectal cancer  
  either to preoperative radiotherapy (5 Gy on each of five days) followed by total mesorectal excision (924 patients)  
